# SvelteKit-side env — this is essentially all you need here. Convex's own
# connection details (PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL, PUBLIC_CONVEX_SITE_URL,
# CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT) are written to .env.local automatically by
# `npx convex dev` — don't hand-edit them there, and don't add them here.
#
# Everything else (WALLET_SIGNING_SECRET, BETTER_AUTH_SECRET, SITE_URL,
# TRUSTED_ORIGINS) is a CONVEX environment variable, set with
# `npx convex env set NAME value` — not a SvelteKit .env file, since these
# are only ever read inside Convex functions. See README.md's
# "Environment variables" section for the full list and what each is for.

# --- Legacy Supabase build (preserved for reference only — see
# supabase/migrations/ and src/lib/server/. Not read by any live route;
# the backend has fully migrated to Convex. Safe to leave unset.) ---
# PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
